Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Driven-SQUID Toric Code: Testing What the Certificate Takes on Trust\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->171623919,ExpressionUUID->"dc0d638f-8bc6-4bc0-8708-6b2e6b60fb95"],

Cell["Mohammad Bahrami \[Bullet] 2026", "Author",
 CellID->1606804240,ExpressionUUID->"9782f3ed-9a53-4da7-8965-e3242e0c63c2"],

Cell["\<\
The preprint arXiv:2611.03329 proposes a method for verifying that a proposed \
device design reproduces a quantum error-correcting code at low energy, \
before the device is built; its test case is the toric code. For the toric \
code, the device Hamiltonian must have four lowest eigenstates, separated \
from all others by an energy gap, spanning a space close to the code's \
protected space up to a fixed rotation of each qubit. AI agents search the \
device parameters and simulate the device, and the Lean proof checker \
certifies that the difference between the simulated Hamiltonian and the ideal \
one, plus a declared numerical tolerance, is too small to close the gap. The \
certificate starts from the Pauli coefficients of the effective Hamiltonian, \
which come from the simulation: it verifies neither the circuit model behind \
these coefficients nor whether the tolerance covers the simulation's \
numerical error, and the authors cover both by human review. This notebook \
tests that model with exact formulas: the coupler's Josephson cosine is \
exactly a sum of 16 Pauli products with closed-form coefficients. The \
formulas reproduce the preprint's simulated four-qubit coupling, and find \
five things the certificate does not test: through the transmon formulas, the \
single coupler's parameters break a condition the preprint sets for the \
eight-qubit array; the main text and the supplement write different Josephson \
terms, and with the supplement's the four-qubit term linear in the drive \
vanishes; the drive makes some unwanted transitions resonant at the listed \
frequencies; a small unwanted term can still split or rotate the protected \
states; and one excitation in the coupler reverses the sign of the four-qubit \
term.\
\>", "Abstract",
 CellID->1787170966,ExpressionUUID->"f7ab9184-dc15-453b-acc4-692d0b07a48d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Question: What Does the Certificate Take on Trust?", "Section",
 CellID->1617143183,ExpressionUUID->"a2b242b5-89b6-410c-9193-a55abe0407d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The preprint arXiv:2611.03329 [1] proposes a method for verifying that a \
proposed device design reproduces a quantum error-correcting code at low \
energy, before the device is built. A quantum error-correcting code stores a \
few qubits in the joint state of many physical qubits, so that an error on \
one physical qubit can be detected and undone. The preprint's test case is \
the toric code on eight qubits, which stores two. The toric code is specified \
by a Hamiltonian, the target Hamiltonian, a sum of eight four-qubit Pauli \
products, products of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fa50e3ca-391c-4b44-9086-b81773f7acef"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "469a284a-49f1-4fea-bb88-e4a1d17d13de"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a804671-a05b-4f48-be0f-5d9d23788780"],
 " on four qubits. Its four lowest states are separated from all others by an \
energy gap, and they span the protected space: the space that holds the two \
stored qubits. The device is driven periodically, so the method describes it \
by its effective Hamiltonian: the time-independent Hamiltonian that produces \
the same evolution over one drive period as the device does. The method \
verifies that the effective Hamiltonian also has four lowest eigenstates, \
separated from all others by an energy gap, and that they span a space close \
to the protected space, up to a fixed rotation of each qubit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1175228907,ExpressionUUID->"69bb1d05-dbd8-4532-adae-3b647845849c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The eight qubits sit on the edges of a 2\[Times]2 square grid wrapped onto \
a torus. Four of the terms are stars, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "902e03b8-c87f-417f-90ef-be6ab7df00cc"],
 " on the four edges that meet at a vertex, and four are plaquettes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013bf96c-7636-4721-af1f-87d1bc3b652a"],
 " on the four edges around a face. Draw the grid with ",
 Cell[BoxData["TorusGraph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49d5909c-2352-4ad5-86c7-640215e29036"],
 ", number each edge by its qubit in the preprint's supplementary Table S1, \
and label each vertex with its star:"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->1304387619,ExpressionUUID->"52a8230a-fd87-4912-a30f-2f83e9d0d140"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"qubitOf", "[", "L_", "]"}], "[", "i_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Quotient", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Ceiling", "[", 
            RowBox[{"i", "/", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
          "L"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Ceiling", "[", 
            RowBox[{"i", "/", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
          "L"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "L", " ", "r"}], " ", "+", " ", "c", " ", "+", " ", 
      "1", " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"If", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"OddQ", "[", "i", "]"}], ",", " ", "L", ",", " ", "0"}], 
       "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"toricGraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"L_", ",", " ", "opts___"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"TorusGraph", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"L", ",", " ", "L"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"EdgeTaggedGraph", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"VertexList", "[", "g", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"EdgeList", "[", "g", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"qubitOf", "[", "L", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"EdgeCount", "[", "g", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "opts"}],
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"starLabel", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sort", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Last", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"IncidenceList", "[", 
        RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"toricGraph", "[", "2", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"toricGraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"EdgeLabels", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<EdgeTag\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"VertexLabels", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"#", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"starLabel", "[", 
           RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"VertexList", "[", "g", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellID->574432246,ExpressionUUID->"e1619d0b-750d-402f-8b00-8b49e3748923"],

