Cell["\<\
Each edge borders two faces and touches two vertices, so each qubit appears \
in two stars and two plaquettes.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->44134596,ExpressionUUID->"071bef46-e549-4a74-bfaf-bec8129ff598"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the device, each of the eight four-qubit terms comes from its own \
coupler, a superconducting loop driven by a magnetic flux (a dc-SQUID, after \
Sameti et al. [2]), so the eight-qubit device, called the array, has eight \
couplers. AI agents search the device parameters. For each setting they write \
a circuit model of the device: a Hamiltonian for the qubits, the coupler and \
the drive, with each part cut off at a few levels. They solve this model \
numerically over one drive period, which the preprint and this notebook call \
the simulation, compute the effective Hamiltonian from the result, and write \
it as a table of Pauli coefficients, one number for each product of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cbec43fb-0cac-4818-b0e9-5dec3585c1a7"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c30cda48-ac51-4b35-bdac-4da1f070652d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05d27e52-252c-4478-85ce-6496f2a34ff1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4faf0890-4395-479d-8b60-215bca19a53f"],
 " on the qubits. The Lean proof checker, a program that verifies every step \
of a mathematical proof, then certifies that the difference between the \
effective Hamiltonian and the target Hamiltonian is too small to close the \
gap. That checked proof is the certificate. The difference includes a \
declared tolerance for the simulation's numerical error, which the proof \
takes as given. The paper's new ingredient is a sharper bound on the \
difference: Pauli terms that anticommute cannot all reach their largest \
values in the same state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1307007571,ExpressionUUID->"2587b845-ed74-40ab-9c93-f6aa3f5b66a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The certificate starts from these simulated Pauli coefficients, so it is \
only as good as they are. The proof does not test two things: whether the \
simulation solves the circuit model accurately, and whether the circuit model \
describes the real device. The authors say so themselves and leave both \
questions to human review by the usual means ([1], the main-text section \
\"Agentic Derivation and Verification Workflow\"). This notebook is such a \
review, done with exact formulas, so anyone can rerun it. Each four-qubit \
term comes from the coupler's Josephson energy, a cosine of the phase across \
the coupler: the superconducting phase difference across the loop, which \
plays the role that position plays for an oscillator. Each qubit shifts that \
phase in proportion to its Pauli ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "becdb9f2-ef8e-4aee-a28b-038040fc9bd6"],
 ". Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9911a41-b9c0-48ba-95ae-c2d202361501"],
 ", the cosine is exactly a sum of 16 Pauli products with closed-form \
coefficients, so the coupler's effect on its four qubits becomes a formula in \
the circuit parameters."
}], "Text",
 CellID->525944366,ExpressionUUID->"eb03432c-d019-45b5-8177-820cd9506410"],

Cell["\<\
Draw the method's steps as a graph, each arrow pointing from a step to the \
one that uses its result. Black vertices are proved in Lean, open vertices \
are numbers that Lean takes as given, and red marks what this notebook tests:\
\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->56923714,ExpressionUUID->"f208c9a7-dfe3-427f-986a-dc9c0ea0a180"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"flow", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<coupler circuit model\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<one-period simulation\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<one-period simulation\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<coupler Pauli coefficients\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<coupler Pauli coefficients\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<array assembly\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<array assembly\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<bound on the difference, plus tolerance\>\""}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<array assembly\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<Lean check: the certificate\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<bound on the difference, plus tolerance\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<Lean check: the certificate\>\""}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<target Hamiltonian\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<Lean check: the certificate\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<gap theorems\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<Lean check: the certificate\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tested", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<this notebook\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<coupler circuit model\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<this notebook\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<coupler Pauli coefficients\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"proved", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<target Hamiltonian\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<gap theorems\>\"", ",",
      " ", "\"\<Lean check: the certificate\>\""}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"given", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<coupler circuit model\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<one-period simulation\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<coupler Pauli coefficients\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<array assembly\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<bound on the difference, plus tolerance\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Graph", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
    RowBox[{"flow", ",", " ", "tested"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"VertexCoordinates", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<coupler circuit model\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<one-period simulation\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<coupler Pauli coefficients\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<array assembly\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<bound on the difference, plus tolerance\>\"", " ", "->", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Lean check: the certificate\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<target Hamiltonian\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1.3", ",", " ", "2.4"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<gap theorems\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1.3", ",", " ", "1.6"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<this notebook\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "1.3"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"VertexLabels", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Placed", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Name\>\"", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"If", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"MemberQ", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               
               RowBox[{"\"\<this notebook\>\"", ",", 
                " ", "\"\<bound on the difference, plus tolerance\>\""}], 
               "}"}], ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "Before", ",", " ", 
            "After"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
       RowBox[{"proved", ",", " ", "given", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "\"\<this notebook\>\"", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"VertexSize", " ", "->", " ", "0.2"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"VertexLabelStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", "13"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"VertexStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
       RowBox[{"proved", " ", "->", " ", "Black"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
       RowBox[{"given", " ", "->", " ", "White"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<this notebook\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "Red"}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"EdgeStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
       RowBox[{"flow", " ", "->", " ", "Gray"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tested", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Red", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImagePadding", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"250", ",", " ", "200"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"15", ",", " ", "15"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "650"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellID->1498948129,ExpressionUUID->"50675684-5414-40ea-a11b-4e302c1708df"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  NamespaceBox["NetworkGraphics",
   DynamicModuleBox[{Typeset`graph = HoldComplete[
     Graph[{
      "coupler circuit model", "one-period simulation", 
       "coupler Pauli coefficients", "array assembly", 
       "bound on the difference, plus tolerance", 
       "Lean check: the certificate", "target Hamiltonian", "gap theorems", 
       "this notebook"}, {{{1, 2}, {2, 3}, {3, 4}, {4, 5}, {4, 6}, {5, 6}, {7,
        6}, {8, 6}, {9, 1}, {9, 3}}, Null}, {
      AspectRatio -> 1, 
       EdgeStyle -> {
