Cell["\<\
Everything above the Lean check reaches it as numbers. The target Hamiltonian \
and the gap theorems come from the code alone, and the certificate holds for \
whatever coefficients arrive from above. This notebook enters at the top, \
where the coefficients are made from the circuit model.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1393935745,ExpressionUUID->"174c2af6-05b0-4b68-aec5-294116e1afc4"],

Cell["\<\
Applied to the preprint's numbers, the formulas reproduce its simulated \
four-qubit coupling to within a few percent. They also find five things the \
certificate does not test.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->313917289,ExpressionUUID->"1bc576d8-5b1d-4093-b594-6972a108ca94"],

Cell["\<\
The preprint studies one coupler in detail. Each qubit is a transmon, a \
weakly nonlinear superconducting oscillator, and standard formulas relate its \
frequency, its Josephson energy and the phase it adds across the coupler. \
Read through these formulas, the single coupler's parameters break a \
condition the preprint sets for the array: at the two low qubit frequencies, \
the chosen phase needs qubit Josephson energies well below the array's 4.9 \
GHz minimum. The preprint does not list the array's parameters qubit by \
qubit, so whether the array itself passes cannot be decided.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->451134304,ExpressionUUID->"bcd0c03f-2852-41c9-b2cc-5efd87204060"],

Cell["\<\
The main text and the supplement write different Josephson terms. With the \
supplement's version, which it calls schematic, the part of the four-qubit \
term proportional to the drive vanishes at the constant part of the flux that \
the preprint fixes.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->844157360,ExpressionUUID->"fa7edcc5-e5c4-4437-88d8-35142f5a0b69"],

Cell["\<\
At the listed frequencies, some drive tones exactly match the energy of an \
unwanted transition that flips two qubits and excites the coupler, and each \
such transition is coupled far more strongly than the four-qubit term. The \
frequencies are rounded too coarsely to tell whether this holds in the real \
circuit.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1463381688,ExpressionUUID->"b5fb14aa-76c1-4e10-a069-6b9bc50fd398"],

Cell["\<\
The certificate bounds the size of the unwanted terms but not what they do. A \
small term can still split or rotate the four protected states, which \
corrupts the stored qubits. Two terms that each only push states out of the \
protected space can also combine into one that does this. The authors leave \
this for future work; the formulas make it concrete.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->10151855,ExpressionUUID->"01526eb1-16ca-4b4d-99d0-3ee89128c717"],

Cell["\<\
The coupler is itself an oscillator, and if it holds one excitation instead \
of none, the four-qubit term it produces reverses sign.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->905391953,ExpressionUUID->"0f3882d9-3b07-4279-90ce-6573f88c29de"],

Cell["\<\
None of this shows that the simulation or the proof is wrong. The certificate \
starts from the numbers the simulation produced. The formulas show where \
those numbers come from: which parameter values can exist together, which \
terms the drive can produce, and what each term does to the stored qubits. \
That is the part the certificate takes on trust, and the part this notebook \
tests.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->430045044,ExpressionUUID->"64790904-5289-4419-a28a-12f94167ba0e"],

Cell["\<\
The notebook first derives the formulas and compares them with the preprint's \
simulated four-qubit coupling. It then takes the five findings in turn, each \
as a question. Can the single coupler's parameters be carried into the \
eight-qubit array? Do the two written Josephson terms describe the same \
device? What else does the drive produce? What does each unwanted term do to \
the stored qubits? And what happens to the four-qubit term when the coupler \
holds an excitation? An appendix tests the formulas a second, independent way.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->234837243,ExpressionUUID->"c1c4089f-0d1c-41fb-8b34-104d56711125"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["How to Read This Notebook", "Section",
 CellID->199760013,ExpressionUUID->"928848b6-cb9c-45a4-aea0-60db1541a5d7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If I cannot compute it, I cannot claim to understand it. So every claim \
below is followed by the code that computes it, and most of that code is an \
exact test that returns ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1271fb9a-1b8c-4a9f-a3d3-304e7389ade8"],
 " or a closed form. Evaluate the inputs from top to bottom, because later \
inputs use earlier definitions. Read each output and what it means first, and \
the code second. Then change a parameter and see which conclusions move."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1072894386,ExpressionUUID->"07a4e22e-3ef8-49cf-ae74-3dc964fa53c2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All energies are divided by Planck's constant, so they are frequencies. \
Qubit and coupler frequencies are in GHz, the Josephson energy ",
 Cell[BoxData["EJ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55ae10aa-33e7-4af8-a94d-1ce023704032"],
 " and the couplings are in kHz, and the drive period is in ns. The circuit \
parameters are those of the preprint's single coupler ([1], Table I), entered \
as exact fractions, so decimals appear only when a result is compared with \
the paper. One more number, ",
 Cell[BoxData["EJqMin"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2064be4c-b486-4d5d-9e2d-fd48206e305c"],
 ", is the 4.9 GHz minimum that the preprint sets for every qubit's Josephson \
energy in the eight-qubit array ([1], supplementary Table S5); Question 1 \
uses it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1333411129,ExpressionUUID->"1e9c6ce1-2018-4665-b440-3b07e929f049"],

Cell["\<\
The circuit model throughout is the preprint's single coupler: four two-level \
qubits and the coupler's lower oscillation mode. Within that model the \
formulas are exact. The preprint's simulation includes more: the shift of \
every level caused by the linear coupling between qubits and coupler, the \
coupler's second mode, the full time evolution over one drive period, and the \
terms that neighboring couplers produce together ([1], \"Single cell \
demonstration\", and supplementary Sec. S6). So the formulas are benchmarks \
and constraints the simulation should satisfy, not a replacement for it. \
Where a further approximation matters, the question that uses it says so.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1825142838,ExpressionUUID->"31034366-b920-4800-a13a-d8e01beb02f2"],

Cell["\<\
Load QuantumFramework and its QEC layer (the development version of its \
quantum error correction tools) from the local copy.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->990404510,ExpressionUUID->"132c7648-6baa-4ed4-81f2-42c6252db714"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$repo", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Quiet", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Check", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ParentDirectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", 
      " ", "\"\</Users/mauriceengelhard/Documents/REPOS/QuantumFramework\>\""}\
], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"PacletDirectoryLoad", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"$repo", ",", " ", "\"\<QuantumFramework\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Get", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "$repo", ",", " ", "\"\<OngoingProjects\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<QEC\>\"", ",",
       " ", "\"\<QECCore\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<QECCore.wl\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}],
    "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QEC`\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0d28f5b7-c00b-4a59-ac4b-b1fabfd49a9a"],

Cell["\<\
This version runs on the current QEC layer, where a code family's parameters \
go inside its name (QECCode[\"CSS\"[hx, hz]], QECCode[\"Toric\"[L]]). Pauli \
products are turned into matrices by QECPauli, which builds the sparse matrix \
directly instead of going through QuantumOperator; this is what makes the \
second-order sums of Question 4 fast. Everything else is the original \
computation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a75cf969-8e05-4113-be3e-aa9488ed14ee"],

Cell["Set the circuit parameters of Table I.", "Text",
 CellID->1245419701,ExpressionUUID->"4d98d9b1-8c0e-4b07-bd6a-923bcbe79c07"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"params", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"<|", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<EJ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"10", "^", "7"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<A\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"47", "/", "10000"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<phizpf\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"165", "/", "100"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<phi\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"7", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<s\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<wq\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"138", ",", " ", "130", ",", " ", "35", ",", " ", "41"}], 
        "}"}], "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<wminus\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"845", "/", "100"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<tones\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "2", ",", " ", "14", ",", " ", "68", ",", " ", "84", ",", " ", "192", 
         ",", " ", "262", ",", " ", "274", ",", " ", "344"}], "}"}], "/", 
       "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<EJqMin\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"49", "/", "10"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<period\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "10"}]}], "|>"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellID->365704094,ExpressionUUID->"b32649db-d55f-45af-8d51-a7f1f5dd0d03"],

Cell["Set the unit conversions from GHz to kHz and MHz.", "Text",
 CellID->1750990038,ExpressionUUID->"bec9cf01-fb8b-4cb2-8d84-2a50b62c99ab"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kHzPerGHz", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"10", "^", "6"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mhzPerGHz", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"10", "^", "3"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellID->84727264,ExpressionUUID->"ec93496e-f64a-4f33-b180-c0053fa479d4"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->728999986,ExpressionUUID->"f0933711-b6d3-4446-9252-b4f548643b46"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Where the Four-Qubit Term Comes From, and Does It Match the Simulation?\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1180044206,ExpressionUUID->"5fa3db63-4ee2-4f55-a297-e1f577b40e2f"],

Cell["\<\
Everything in the preprint's device rests on one term. Its main text writes \
the coupler's Josephson energy as\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->378596892,ExpressionUUID->"f18bcb6a-ec1e-4b3b-8d2a-ecac99ba4ebf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["J", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"d", "c"}], "TI"]], "+", 
      SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"]]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "^"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1324119915,ExpressionUUID->"650734da-0020-4544-8485-fa48d9faa7a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["J", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4f641d2-b071-4ff4-a396-ebbdf189a674"],
 " is the Josephson energy of each junction and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "c"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a3f73c1c-fb7d-4eb6-bc93-18cc915f576a"],
 " is a static flux bias ([1], \"Single cell demonstration\"). The drive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1673849d-96e4-4833-9cc1-02ac77175179"],
 " is a sum of eight tones, each with amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "85bfeb92-0c98-4a85-952f-18a8dfc5e864"],
 ". The operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d57989de-ea5a-4fc6-a91b-803758a8248e"],
 " is the phase across the coupler. This section asks three things. What in \
this term produces a four-qubit coupling? How strong is that coupling? And \
does it match the preprint's simulation?"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1978785535,ExpressionUUID->"ab089f0e-1c0b-4517-b46c-c60eafaef2ea"],

Cell["\<\
The phase across the coupler has two parts: the coupler's own oscillation, \
and a shift from each qubit ([1], same section).\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2016628702,ExpressionUUID->"e70a3feb-91d0-4b79-a6d8-134575939123"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "^"], "=", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "=", "1"}], "4",
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", 
      StyleBox["zpf",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["d", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "/", 
      RowBox[{"2", "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->96606702,ExpressionUUID->"2b54297e-5a8d-4594-96db-83a13c644232"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca5678fe-f62a-4ba5-9b68-a209f8a49160"],
 " removes one excitation from the coupler, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", 
   StyleBox["zpf",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "152f10a3-d469-4993-9455-28cf153e9cfe"],
 " is the size of the coupler's zero-point phase fluctuation. The \
participation phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5086c505-998d-4a83-b9e4-d2e82b8f4639"],
 " is how much phase qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3243ef25-9f4d-4e57-8b13-cbaaf094810f"],
 " adds when it changes state, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f89a1618-985d-4308-84d3-a84a3eb464d9"],
 " is the sign of its connection."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1721132978,ExpressionUUID->"af28b7d2-3197-4cfc-bc9c-931b185cbe51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The cosine of an operator is normally an infinite series. Here it is not. \
Each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "98d08605-3a47-4104-ac14-b7ea30b95718"],
 " squares to the identity, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"]}]], "=", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c0d4bf85-7341-496e-a82e-e476c09afc1c"],
 ", and"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2121435355,ExpressionUUID->"da70ae0a-f98b-4d48-860b-ee83c849e527"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "^"]}]], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}]], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "+", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1035562367,ExpressionUUID->"9237d0be-c362-4098-a0a5-83628ede021f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Multiplying out the product gives 16 terms, one for each set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b844ef0a-8e31-40f7-8001-cdc26631f9a9"],
 " of qubits. Each term is the Pauli product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bc8c6d68-ae29-46f1-9baf-168b0704d2e9"],
 ", with a factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8408cbda-0d09-42b1-b62d-4a9ee91794dd"],
 " for every qubit in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "80dc53f6-6742-4dc3-9e5d-ee9b74c25139"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee17d9a5-a547-4209-b8fb-64184e212dd7"],
 " for every qubit outside it. The cosine keeps the real part. In the code, \
",
 Cell[BoxData["t1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba190f1b-1e74-4318-88e8-0410d57b94db"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData["t4"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e715d437-137a-4355-8c42-5258eb29d176"],
 " are the four angles ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ab42a8ee-01cb-4bbf-8896-15929db6f1fc"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1623037933,ExpressionUUID->"6346faf0-2761-46ba-8380-349e7642da3b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the coefficient of every Pauli product in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b98bf1e0-86ad-4f16-8cae-1ca338670a78"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1723954199,ExpressionUUID->"3dd87bc7-07e2-44ba-ad7a-58e2241886fa"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"angles", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", "t2", ",", " ", "t3", ",", " ", "t4"}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xFactor", "[", "s_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ReplacePart", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "angles", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
       RowBox[{"s", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"angles", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "s", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"coef", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Cos", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "a"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"xFactor", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"coef", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Sin", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Im", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "a"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"xFactor", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"#", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"coef", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Cos", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellID->76814079,ExpressionUUID->"f8d50f25-74c5-4925-8933-8231f387f1e2"],

