Cell["\<\
Even the rounding of the coupler frequency alone allows detunings far larger \
than the couplings. So the listed frequencies can neither establish nor \
exclude these resonances. The unrounded frequencies, and the shifted levels \
the simulation actually uses, decide them.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2105419012,ExpressionUUID->"220adf95-a124-43a8-8158-1ee8eeeaf72c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Can the Drive's Energy Shifts Explain the Preprint's Largest Unwanted Term?\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1004868130,ExpressionUUID->"552c5aca-521b-4348-a577-489dd71c69b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Transitions that are not resonant still matter, because each shifts the \
energy of the configuration it starts from. The preprint reports its largest \
unwanted driven term for the single coupler only by size: 11.4% of the \
four-qubit term, about 9.22 kHz. It does not say which Pauli product that \
term multiplies ([1], \"Single cell demonstration\"). So the comparison is \
with every coefficient the energy shifts produce. At the listed frequencies \
they all stay below it. Products of two or more ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5251fc93-6697-4f81-a409-cf46d3ca1c10"],
 " stay far below, and only the single-qubit shifts come within a factor of a \
few."
}], "Text",
 CellID->610416584,ExpressionUUID->"7ffc4238-493e-45e2-ae32-5955ebb46449"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At second order, a transition with coupling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["g", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f26d07ad-542c-42c7-9d1e-331b85c67460"],
 " and detuning ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalDelta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e62c7761-1372-4a91-9054-1dfef479504e"],
 " shifts its starting configuration by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], "2"], "/", "\[CapitalDelta]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6bb5e95-a1ea-4a04-8eb8-e6e09307717f"],
 ". The 16 shifted energies of the four qubits can be rewritten exactly as a \
constant plus 15 products of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3a462e5-3cb4-4a58-a5a6-1bab17d4ac59"],
 " operators, the qubits' version of a Fourier series over their 16 \
configurations. The exactly resonant transitions above are left out, because \
they need a different treatment."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2115927446,ExpressionUUID->"cda0db91-f81a-43bb-8b06-9555c0385a86"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Recover the shift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], "2"], "/", "\[CapitalDelta]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bc5b4994-6ff6-4900-8042-f28ea55173b6"],
 " from an exactly solvable two-level system, for positive detuning."
}], "Text",
 CellID->753099453,ExpressionUUID->"2d3a562b-03b3-405a-a29a-3743180e842a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"d", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"d", "^", "2"}], "/", "4"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"g", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"d", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellID->1406782960,ExpressionUUID->"e937ba07-9ca7-499b-a5f3-fc8f4bf29d02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"-", 
  FractionBox[
   SuperscriptBox["g", "2"], "d"]}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"aacd59a3-15b2-\
4586-88fb-ef225ea850b1"]
}, Open  ]],

