 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"1a43a5b3-f37d-45bd-a781-ef98dee4af81"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Dropping the transitions that are not safely detuned changes both the largest \
single-qubit and the largest multi-qubit coefficient by a sizable fraction, \
so the listed frequencies settle neither. In both sums, though, every \
coefficient stays below the preprint's 9.22 kHz. At the unrounded \
frequencies, a transition that is not safely detuned could lie closer to \
resonance and shift its configuration more.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1968964190,ExpressionUUID->"679f1a62-3316-49e4-8a26-dc4f94de7f24"],

Cell["\<\
The comparison is rough for a second reason. The preprint removes the \
one-body phases that a frame update can compensate before it extracts its \
Hamiltonian, and it extracts that Hamiltonian from one period of evolution of \
the dressed states ([1], supplementary Sec. S4). So single-qubit shifts like \
these need not appear in its table at all. A direct comparison needs the same \
conventions on both sides.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->157436911,ExpressionUUID->"f8913149-e766-4cfe-ba42-056cdca874f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Second order also has transitions that change the qubit configuration \
through two tones at once, or through one tone used twice. Before computing \
their strengths, ask which are allowed at all. The rule found with the \
coupler factor says the cosine changes the number of coupler excitations and \
the number of flipped qubits together by an even amount. So from an empty \
coupler a transition needs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a07e9a0d-1e26-461d-a11c-5d56423243ef"],
 " even. Energy matching alone would include forbidden transitions."
}], "Text",
 CellID->158497134,ExpressionUUID->"9b49dc50-3a39-425f-8633-34a7fd028ea1"],

Cell["\<\
Find the transitions that match the sum or difference of any two tones, the \
same tone twice included, and are allowed by this rule.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->273736603,ExpressionUUID->"a96a93e7-6e52-45da-ae3d-d16fc1f25c0a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"twoTone", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DeleteCases", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Union", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Total", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"params", "[", "\"\<tones\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", 
            RowBox[{"params", "[", "\"\<tones\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
         " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"twoToneCandidates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"zStates", ",", " ", "zWords", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "mMax"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"z_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "m_"}], "}"}], " ", "/;", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"EvenQ", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "s", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
       "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"MemberQ", "[", 
        RowBox[{"twoTone", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"energyChange", "[", 
          RowBox[{"z", ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", "m"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellID->1934379342,ExpressionUUID->"b04c6da2-0040-47a6-93f5-9a9dd33b3042"],

Cell["Count them.", "Text",
 CellID->429948480,ExpressionUUID->"e568bf7c-bd1c-4195-a3ff-6da7034ed07c"],

